h probability, and that this matches the ranking implied by the decision reason (B > A), and assuming the reason is interpreted as comparing the smaller of the two probabilities (i.e., the rare event, which is the win), the reasoning aligns. Therefore, the information considered (probability of winning) matches the relevant information for the reason, and the justification (higher chance to win) aligns with preferring the lottery with higher minimum probability if we equate 'minimum probability' with the smaller of the two probabilities in each lottery (33% vs 34%).",
